  rhythms your digestion hormone  production cognition and more here's  what my temperature looks like  throughout the day  other bodily cycles like ovulation can  cause small swings in temperature - and  different parts of you are different  temperatures under the tongue armpit  forehead and rectal readings are all  likely to be unique point is there are  tons of variables we can be many  temperatures all at once  all the time and still be perfectly  healthy but being sick is another story  so I spoke with a couple people who are  connecting some interesting dots between  temperature variation and an illness  like Ovid 19 when you get sick many of  your body's natural predictable rhythms  start to destabilize your temperature  might fluctuate more erratically and it  might crank up above your natural range  that's your body triggering a fever to  make itself less hospitable to viruses  or bacteria in other words your body  temperature gets anomalous that's  trouble for you but for people tracking  kovat it's crucial data one effort is  kinsa a company that tracks the spread  of infectious disease using fevers kinsa  cells a smart thermometer that sends  your temperature back to the company  every time you take it Kenseth says they  have about a million thermometers in  circulation and with all that data  they've built a real-time health weather  map it shows possible hot spots of Kovan  counties with more fever than flu season  would explain let's take our real-time  signal and remove the expected value  cold and flu what's left over is a  residual that residual is atypical and  in this particular analysis a typical  fever clusters things that you would not  expect what we found since that point is  that there's a very high correlation  between our hot spots in koban 19 cases  the work is not peer reviewed yet and  some experts question how reliable it  can be with only a million thermometers  their user base could also be biased by  race or class or other factors 